      "message": "nit: you could allocate the size of this array upfront since you know futureCount. that would avoid several promises.push operations.\n\n\nanother thing you can do is temporarily store an array at `WebGPU._promisesTempList` which you reuse. That helps avoid re-allocating new lists.\n\nso it can look something like:\n\n```\nvar promises \u003d WebGPU._promisesTempList;\npromises.length \u003d futureCount + (needTimeout ? 1 : 0);\n...\nvar anyPromise \u003d Promise.any(promises);\nreturn Asyncify.handleAsync(() \u003d\u003e anyPromise);\n```",
